from pathlib import Path
import re,json,shutil
root=Path.cwd(); work=root/'build/tf2-site';work.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
changed=[]
def write(relative,text):
 p=root/relative;p.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
 if p.exists():
  old=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
  if old==text:return
  backup=work/'before'/(relative+'.bak');backup.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
  if not backup.exists():backup.write_bytes(p.read_bytes())
 p.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8',newline='');changed.append(relative)
def edit(relative,before,after):
 s=(root/relative).read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
 if before not in s:raise ValueError('Missing edit anchor: '+relative+' '+before[:60])
 write(relative,s.replace(before,after,1))
topics=[
('getting-started','Getting started','Set up the free TF2 preview, choose your edition and open the menu.',
'''<ol><li><a href="/download/">Download Scooby Launcher</a> and sign in. Both TF2 editions are free for signed-in users; no separate TF2 purchase is needed.</li><li>Open <strong>TF2</strong> from Home or Source Games. Choose <strong>Team Fortress 2</strong> for retail, or <strong>TF2 Classified</strong> for Classified, then select <strong>Continue</strong>.</li><li>Enable <strong>Start game</strong> and press <strong>Load</strong>. The loader starts the selected Steam game with <code>-insecure</code> and waits for it to become ready. If the game is already open, it must have been started with that launch option.</li><li>Start a local practice/listen-server map. The current native features and Lua game queries require an eligible local session.</li><li>Press <strong>Insert</strong> or <strong>F1</strong> to open the menu. Start with a few settings and save a profile once you are happy with them.</li></ol><figure class="tf2-guide-figure"><img src="/assets/images/tf2/edition-picker.png" alt="Scooby Launcher’s TF2 edition picker with retail and Classified cards, a Don’t show again toggle and Continue button." width="1000" height="800" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Choose an edition before opening its dashboard.</figcaption></figure><h3>Using an edition ZIP</h3><p>Extract the whole archive and keep its <code>TF2</code> folder beside <code>ScoobyLoader.exe</code>. Each ZIP includes the files for its named edition. The loader verifies the package before use. Use a matching package from the official download flow when updating.</p><p>For a missing menu or a game that stays on “Waiting for game,” follow <a href="/guides/tf2/troubleshooting/">troubleshooting</a>.</p>'''),
('requirements','Requirements','Check your game edition, Windows architecture, account and session before loading.',
'''<ul><li><strong>Windows x64</strong> and the matching 64-bit Steam game installation.</li><li><strong>A signed-in Scooby session.</strong> Both editions currently use free access.</li><li><strong>The current loader and matching TF2 package.</strong> An older package can reject a newer game build.</li><li><strong>The <code>-insecure</code> launch option.</strong> Start game supplies it automatically. For an already-running game, close it, add the option in Steam’s game properties, and restart.</li><li><strong>A local practice/listen-server session.</strong> Remote-server gameplay is outside the current supported session path.</li></ul><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Edition</th><th>Expected game process</th><th>Steam game</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Team Fortress 2</td><td><code>tf_win64.exe</code></td><td>440</td></tr><tr><td>TF2 Classified</td><td><code>tf2classified_win64.exe</code></td><td>3545060</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Preview support</h3><p>The TF2 family is a preview. Full feature parity and every weapon, entity and game transition have not been verified. Linux, Proton and 32-bit game builds are not validated for this package. Check the selected game’s compatibility after a game update.</p><p><a href="/guides/tf2/getting-started/">Continue to setup →</a></p>'''),
('editions','TF2 or TF2 Classified','Choose the correct game and keep the loader’s selection and your game data in sync.',
'''<div class="tf2-edition-guide"><article><img src="/assets/images/tf2/tf2-logo-transparent-v1.png" alt="Team Fortress 2" width="739" height="249"><h3>Team Fortress 2</h3><p>The default selection for the original Steam game. Retail has its own world and mode controls, including Mann vs. Machine features where supported.</p></article><article><img src="/assets/images/tf2/tf2-classified-logo.png" alt="TF2 Classified" width="500" height="148"><h3>TF2 Classified</h3><p>A separate game installation and package. Its host recognizes the four-team layout and Civilian class; scripts can check these capabilities.</p></article></div><h3>Remember your choice</h3><p>Choose a card and select <strong>Continue</strong>. <strong>Don’t show again</strong> skips the popup on later visits. Cancel, Escape and the close button leave your saved choice unchanged.</p><h3>Switch later</h3><p>Use <strong>Game version</strong> in the TF2 dashboard to switch editions. The logo, target game and files change with the selection. Turn <strong>Version popup</strong> back on to show the chooser again.</p><p>Each edition keeps its own settings, scripts and game process. Switching the dashboard does not transfer profiles or unload a module from a game that is already open. Restart the relevant game before replacing or reloading its module.</p><p><a href="/products/tf2/?edition=tf2-classified">View the Classified product preview →</a></p>'''),
('menu-settings','Menu settings and profiles','Adjust the interface, visuals, keybinds and edition-specific settings.',
'''<p>Use <strong>Insert</strong> or <strong>F1</strong> to open or close the menu. The interface starts with main tabs at the top and subtabs at the bottom; later layout changes are saved.</p><ul><li><strong>Combat:</strong> separate Rage and Legit profiles, with their own activation controls. Set an aim or trigger key and choose Hold, Toggle or Always.</li><li><strong>ESP:</strong> configure Enemy and Friendly players independently. Use the gear beside the player preview for class and team appearance. Item, building and world controls depend on the edition.</li><li><strong>Chams:</strong> choose a target and configure Visible, Invisible and Overlay layers separately, including each layer’s color.</li><li><strong>View and Movement:</strong> camera/model FOV and movement controls live in their named pages. Additional controls differ between editions.</li><li><strong>Settings:</strong> adjust menu scale, language and appearance, then save a named configuration under Configs.</li><li><strong>Lua:</strong> run a bundled example or edit a script. See the <a href="/guides/tf2/lua-scripts/">Lua guide</a>.</li></ul><h3>Keep your profiles</h3><p>Native user data is separate from downloaded packages:</p><ul><li>Retail: <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Scooby\\TF2</code></li><li>Classified: <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Scooby\\TF2 Classified</code></li></ul><p>Use the menu’s folder controls to locate editable scripts and profiles. Back up your edition’s user-data folder before replacing a setup. The loader’s Open folder action opens its package/cache location, which is separate from your in-game profile data.</p><h3>Stopping</h3><p>The product’s <strong>Stop</strong> action disables its active hooks and restores owned input/render state. Restart the game before loading another build. Stopping an individual Lua script removes its callbacks and script UI; changes it made to built-in settings remain.</p>'''),
('lua-scripts','Lua scripts','Run examples in either edition and use the shared TF2 host API.',
'''<ol><li>Open the menu’s <strong>Lua / Scripts</strong> manager or <strong>Lua Editor</strong>.</li><li>Choose a bundled example such as <strong>TF2 Player HUD.lua</strong> or <strong>TF2 Player Labels.lua</strong>. Examples do not run automatically.</li><li>Open the script in the editor and select <strong>Run</strong>. A HUD example needs an eligible local session with a local player; it can correctly draw nothing at the main menu.</li><li>Use the editor’s <strong>Stop</strong> control to unload that script before making changes or rerunning it.</li><li>Open <strong>API docs</strong> beside the editor for signatures and examples. The <a href="/api/tf2/">website API reference</a> is searchable too.</li></ol><h3>One script, two editions</h3><p>Use <code>tf2</code> in scripts shared between retail and Classified. Classified also supplies <code>tf2c</code> as an alias. <code>tf2.info()</code> returns <code>tf2</code> or <code>tf2_classified</code> as the game ID; <code>tf2.capabilities()</code> and <code>tf2.has_feature(id)</code> let you check edition-specific behavior.</p><h3>Safe empty results</h3><p>Check for <code>nil</code> before reading a local player or projection result. Game queries become empty when there is no eligible local session, during a transition, or after Stop. Read a fresh snapshot inside each callback.</p><p><a href="/docs/tf2/">Download examples and start scripting →</a></p><p>Copying scripts into an old build does not add a newer host API. Use the version and function names supplied by your installed TF2 package.</p>'''),
('troubleshooting','Troubleshooting','Resolve edition selection, loading, missing menu, empty data and script errors.',
'''<h3>The loader cannot find my game</h3><p>Check Game version first: retail and Classified have different executables. Close duplicate instances of the selected game. Start that edition through the dashboard, or restart it through Steam with <code>-insecure</code>. Wait for the game to reach its menu before retrying.</p><h3>The game changed after an update</h3><p>Use the latest matching TF2 package. The native adapter checks the supported game build and can reject changed modules. Do not substitute files from the other edition; wait for a compatible update when the current build is unsupported.</p><h3>The package is incomplete or fails verification</h3><p>Extract the complete official ZIP again into a fresh folder, keeping its TF2 directory beside the loader. For server downloads, check your connection and retry. Keep your user-data backup; replacing a runtime package does not require deleting profiles.</p><h3>Loaded, but the menu does not appear</h3><p>Focus the game and try Insert or F1. Read the loader’s exact status. If it reports that startup did not accept the session, restart the game and sign in again before retrying. A loaded library alone does not prove that every gameplay feature is active.</p><h3>ESP or Lua queries show no data</h3><p>Enter an eligible local practice/listen-server map and wait for a live local player. Check feature toggles, team/category filters and ranges. In the API, inspect <code>tf2.session()</code>; empty results are expected while disconnected, after Stop or in an ineligible session.</p><h3>A model preview is empty</h3><p>Class-preview models depend on locally generated game assets and are not included in the public runtime ZIPs. A missing preview mesh does not identify a Lua error or an edition mismatch.</p><h3>A script reports an error</h3><p>Open the Lua console, check the named line and function, and compare the example with <a href="/api/tf2/">the TF2 API</a>. Check nil results and API version 1.0. Stop the script, correct it and run it again. Script callbacks and UI are cleaned up when the script is stopped.</p><p>For further help, include your edition, loader message, reproduction steps and the relevant console error. Avoid sharing passwords, keys or session data.</p>''')
]
